+### Clean Code (MEDIUM unless noted)
+
+Check new and changed code only. For untouched code add at most one line in total ("noticed: ..."), never a refactor request, and never ask to rewrite existing code to meet the numbers below. First read the project's size card: Grep `^## Розмір` in the root CLAUDE.md, CLAUDE.local.md and AGENTS.md with 8 lines of context (level T0-T3, «Не додаємо», «Люки»); no card means no level checks. The project's own conventions win over the numbers below.
+
+- **Duplicate of existing code**: a new helper, component, constant or block of 8+ lines that already exists in the repo. Grep the new name and one or two distinctive lines and cite the existing location. Fix: call or import the existing one (export it if needed). Changing the existing code (new parameter, move to a shared module) is a suggestion for the owner, not a required fix.
+- **Grown giant**: the diff creates a file over 400 lines, adds a new responsibility to a file over 400 lines, pushes a file past 800, adds a function or hook over 100 lines, a component over 200 lines or with 10+ `useState`, or adds a new branch inline to an existing function over 100 lines. Fix: a new module, hook or subcomponent next to it. Skip exhaustive `switch`, config objects, test tables and generated code.
+- **Deep nesting**: more than 3 levels in new code. Fix: early returns, extract a helper.
+- **Mixed I/O and logic**: one new function does I/O (HTTP, DB, files) and also 10+ lines of calculation or mapping that could be a pure function.
+- **Speculative abstraction**: a new interface, factory, generic helper, wrapper or layer with one implementation and one caller, unless the neighbouring modules already use that pattern (for example `service` and `repository` per module) or it is a «Люки» item of the size card.
+- **Excluded by the size card** (HIGH, quote the card line as the proof): the diff adds something the card's «Не додаємо» line names (for example Redis, a broker, a package, a repository layer), and the review request does not say the owner approved it.
+- **Dead code left by the diff**: imports, exports, functions or variables the change made unused; commented-out code; new exports nothing imports. Name unused files, do not ask to delete them.
+- **Naming** (LOW): generic names outside tests (`tmp`, `obj`, `data2`, `res2`), booleans without `is/has/can`, a unit missing from the name (`timeout` instead of `timeoutMs`), a new name for a domain term the repo already names.
+- **Magic values** (LOW): business limits, timeouts or thresholds as bare literals; MEDIUM when the same value appears in 2+ places.
+- **What-comments** (LOW): comments that restate the code instead of saying why.
+
